      "reasoning": "If I swing all, my opponent has Baneslayer Angel (5/5 tapped), Emancipation Angel (3/3), Gonti (2/3), Masked Blackguard (2/1), Mausoleum Turnkey (3/2 sick - can't attack but can block).\n\
My Baneslayer problem requires me to survive. Since it's Baneslayer (Lifelink, First Strike, Flying), it blocks profitably, but right now it is *tapped* because it attacked me.\n\
Wait, Baneslayer was tapped? Baneslayer Angel does *not* have vigilance. So it's tapped!\n\
Wait! Emancipation Angel (3/3), Gonti (2/3), Masked Blackguard (2/1), Mausoleum Turnkey (3/2 sick) are untapped.\n\
I am at 10 HP. I can attack with Rampaging Baloths (6/6), 4/4 Beast, three 2/2 Elementals, Courser (2/4), Rager (2/2).\n\
If I swing 6/6 and 4/4 and a ton of other things, I will take out some of their creatures, but they might just double block. Since I need to survive the crackback from Baneslayer (5 damage, I go to 5), Emancipation Angel (3 damage, I go to 2). So I need to keep some blockers to block their non-flyers. Or, actually, Baneslayer and Emancipation Angel both fly. I CANNOT BLOCK THEM with anything except if I have reach/flying. Courser doesn't have reach. Do I have anything with flying/reach? No.\n\
Next turn they attack with Baneslayer (5) and Emancip. Angel (3), that's 8 flying damage. If I swing, I need to make sure I don't die next turn.\n\
I will pass attacks so I can block their ground creatures. Actually I will be at 2 life, so I should keep blockers. Wait, if I attack with everything I might deal huge damage.\n\
Let's just pass attacks.",
