      "reasoning": "I am taking 5+3+2+2+3 = 15 damage. I have to block enough to not die.\n\
I have Baneslayer Angel (5/5 flying), Emancipation Angel (3/3 flying), Gonti (2/3 deathtouch), Masked Blackguard (2/1), Mausoleum Turnkey (3/2). I can't block the flyers! So I'm taking 5+3 = 8 damage in the air. I have 10 life. So I will go to 2. Wait, I also need to make sure I don't lose to the 5 damage on the ground.\n\
Wait... what is on the stack? \"Ability\". What ability triggers when they attack? Masked Blackguard or something? No... wait, does one of their creatures trigger? Ah, \"when this creature attacks\". Since neither Baneslayer nor Emancipation Angel triggers... maybe Mausoleum Turnkey doesn't. Gonti doesn't. Let me checking Oracle text for Masked Blackguard. \"When you control another Rogue, this gets something\"? Masked Blackguard is a 2/1. Let's block the 3 ground creatures. I'll take 8 from the flyers and drop to 2 life.\n\
Gonti (2/3 deathtouch) -> block with a 2/2 Elemental token.\n\
Masked Blackguard (2/1) -> block with a 2/2 Elemental token.\n\
Mausoleum Turnkey (3/2) -> block with a 2/2 Elemental token.\n\
Wait, if they trade I lose three 2/2 tokens but survive the ground assault. I will have plenty of power left on my turn.\n\
Could there be pump spells? Yes. So block Gonti with Courser of Kruphix (2/4)? No, Gonti is deathtouch, it will kill Courser. Best to block Gonti with a tiny token.\n\
I'll block Gonti (id=p74) with Elemental (p62).\n\
Block Masked Blackguard (id=p34) with Elemental (p84).\n\
Block Mausoleum Turnkey (id=p79) with Elemental (p93).",
