I can play a land and trigger:\n\
Courser (gain 1 life) -> I go to 3.\n\
Baloths (make a 4/4 Beast) -> 4 power (has summoning sickness).\n\
Zendikar's Roil (make a 2/2 Elemental) -> 2 power (summoning sickness).\n\
\n\
So I have 22 attacking power and they are at 35. I cannot kill them.\n\
Wait... they have exactly 35 life.\n\
Is there anything in my exile? Malefic Scythe is exiled face down by Gonti. Oh wait, my hand is Broodlings, Swamp, Thriving Moor.\n\
They have no flying blockers but I only have 22 power.\n\
Wait! I am dead next turn to Baneslayer (5) + Emancipation Angel (3) unless I have a reach/flying blocker.\n\
Wait, I have no reach/flying in hand, and my library is what?\n\
Look at my hand: Phyrexian Broodlings (2/2 ground), Swamp, Thriving Moor.\n\
I will play a land, gain 1 life (up to 3).\n\
Wait, if I have Phyrexian Debaser (2/2 flying)... oh wait!\n\
Phyrexian Debaser: 2/2 Flying. Can I block Baneslayer? Yes!\n\
Wait, Baneslayer is 5/5 flying first strike tram... wait no trample. So I can block Baneslayer!\n\
But Emancipation Angel is 3/3 flying. They will still hit me for 3 flying damage, and I am at 3 life! Wait, Courser gains me 1 life. I will be at 3 life. Emancipation Angel hits me for 3 -> I go to 0. So I need to gain 2 life to survive, or block Emancipation Angel with something else.\n\
Can I block Emancipation Angel? I only have 1 flier (Debaser).\n\
Wait! What if I draw a card? But Courser sees the top card of library. Wait, my Courser reveals top card.\n\
Wait, I see the top card of my library because I control Courser! Let's see... my hand says Swamp, so I must have drawn Swamp. What is the new top card? It is not listed in my library on the prompt. Is it in hand? My hand has Swamp.\n\
Wait, if I just play a land (Swamp), I get a 4/4 Beast and a 2/2 Elemental and gain 1 life.\n\
Then if I cast Phyrexian Broodlings `{1}{B}{B}`, I have no flying.\n\
What are my chances?\n\
I can activate Phyrexian Debaser: \"{T}, Sacrifice {this}: Target creature gets -2/-2 until end of turn.\"\n\
Wait! Emancipation Angel is 3/3. Baneslayer is 5/5. Baneslayer has Protection from Demons and Dragons. Phyrexian Debaser is... a Carrier.\n\
Let's check Debaser. I can't kill Emancipation Angel because it gives -2/-2. It becomes a 1/1. Then Baneslayer (5/5) and Emanc (1/1) = 6 damage. My Debaser is gone, so I can't block at all. 6 damage = I'm dead since I only have 3 life.\n\
Wait... Baneslayer is 5. Emancip is 3. If I block Baneslayer with Debaser, Baneslayer deals 0 to me. Then I take 3 from Emancip. 3-3 = 0.\n\
What if I give Baneslayer -2/-2? It becomes 3/3, Emancip 3/3, 6 damage. Dead.\n\
\n\
Can I kill Baneslayer or Emancip Angel? I can't.\n\
Wait, I have 8 untapped lands! I can double spell? I don't have removal.\n\
Wait, what if I can attack for lethal? No, 22 damage vs 35 life.\n\
Wait... they have Gonti, Baneslayer, Emancip Angel tapped. They have NO untapped creatures!\n\
Wait, Baneslayer has lifelink, so they go to 40 if Baneslayer deals damage.\n\
If I attack with everything... wait, can I attack them down to 13, and then...\n\
No, I'm dead next turn regardless since they have Baneslayer and Emancipation Angel and I only have 3 life and 1 blocker (Debaser).\n\
Wait! Look at Debaser. \"Flying. T, Sac: Target creature gets -2/-2.\"\n\
If I play Thriving Moor... wait, does Courser let me see the top of my library? I don't see it in the list.\n\
I should play Swamp now and maybe draw it if I have a draw spell. Rager draws a card but loses 1 life. I don't have Rager in hand.\n\
I'll just pass priority until I die, but I can make the best available plays.\n\
I will play a plain old Swamp.",
