      "reasoning": "Wait, all 3 of their creatures are tapped. I can attack for free with everything that doesn't have a good blocking use.\n\
I must keep Debaser to block Baneslayer (5/5). If I block Baneslayer with Debaser, it deals 5 to Debaser. Baneslayer gives them 5 life. Emancipation Angel (3/3) kills me (3 damage) because I have 3 life.\n\
Wait... if I have 3 life, Emancipation Angel hits me for exactly 3, so I go to 0. I have no flyers other than Debaser. So I am dead next turn!\n\
Unless... what if I attack with everything and they just take it, they go to down. I can't kill them.\n\
Wait, can I force them to block? No, their creatures are tapped.\n\
Wait... is there any way I survive? I can't block Emancipation Angel. Wait! I CAN sacrifice Debaser to give Emancipation Angel -2/-2! Then it's a 1/1. Then it deals 1 damage to me! I go to 2 life!\n\
BUT THEN I can't block Baneslayer! Baneslayer deals 5 damage! 5 + 1 = 6. I'm dead!\n\
Wait... \"Sacrifice a creature\" is Broodlings? Yes, Phyrexian Broodlings: {1}, Sacrifice a creature: Put a +1/+1 counter on {this}.\n\
Broodlings doesn't have flying.\n\
Wait. Emancipation Angel hits for 3. Baneslayer hits for 5. Total 8 damage.\n\
If I have 2 flyers/reach, I can live. I have ZERO reach, ONE flyer.\n\
Is there any other line? I can't interact with their board. I'll attack with all ground creatures, make them think I have a trick, then pass.\n\
Attackers: everything but Debaser.\n\
Rampaging Baloths (p27), Beast (p94), Beast (p102), Courser (p43), Rager (p40), Elemental (p101).\n\
Wait, Rager might as well attack. Ensure I don't attack with Debaser.\n\
IDs: p40, p43, p27, p94, p101, p102.",
